<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#142d4c"><meta name="description" content="Explore assistance programs available in Georgia."><title>Georgia Assistance Programs — American Aid Network</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/google-analytics.php"; ?></head><body><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/site-header.php"; ?><main><section class="state-page"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/help/">Browse Programs</a><span>›</span><b>Georgia</b></div><div class="state-intro"><div><h1>Assistance Programs in Georgia</h1><p>10 programs, grouped by what you need help with. Each includes clear application guidance.</p></div><div><a class="button primary" href="/find/">Find my programs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><small>Free · Private · Takes under 2 minutes</small></div></div><section class="program-group"><h2>Rent &amp; Housing Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>2-1-1 in Georgia (United Way Network)</h3><p>Dial 2-1-1 from any Georgia phone for free, confidential help finding local assistance: food, housing, utility bills, health care, and more. Regional United Way centers answer for their own service areas across the state.</p><div><a href="/programs/2-1-1-in-georgia-united-way-network/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/2-1-1-in-georgia-united-way-network/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Georgia Medicaid</h3><p>Free or low-cost health coverage for eligible Georgia children, pregnant women, seniors, people who are blind or disabled, and some low-income parents. One Georgia Gateway application screens every Medicaid category and PeachCare for Kids together.</p><div><a href="/programs/georgia-medicaid/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/georgia-medicaid/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>GeorgiaLegalAid.org (Eviction &amp; Legal Help)</h3><p>Free plain-language legal information for Georgians on eviction, foreclosure, public benefits, family law, and debt, run by Atlanta Legal Aid and the Georgia Legal Services Program, with self-help forms and a virtual assistant.</p><div><a href="/programs/georgialegalaid-org-eviction-and-legal-help/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/georgialegalaid-org-eviction-and-legal-help/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Food Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Georgia WIC</h3><p>Nutritious foods on an eWIC card, breastfeeding support, health education, and referrals for pregnant women, new mothers, infants, and young children in Georgia. Apply through Georgia Gateway or your county health department; call 800-228-9173 with questions.</p><div><a href="/programs/georgia-wic/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/georgia-wic/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>SNAP Food Stamps (Georgia Gateway)</h3><p>Georgia SNAP puts monthly grocery money on an EBT card. Apply through Georgia Gateway at gateway.ga.gov, where one account also handles Medicaid, TANF, WIC, and child care assistance, or call DFCS at 877-423-4746.</p><div><a href="/programs/snap-food-stamps-georgia-gateway/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/snap-food-stamps-georgia-gateway/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Utility Bill Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>LIHEAP (Energy Assistance)</h3><p>Georgia&#39;s LIHEAP helps income-qualified households pay heating and cooling bills, with crisis help for life-threatening energy emergencies. DFCS funds community action agencies that take applications; seniors 65+ and the medically homebound get an early application window.</p><div><a href="/programs/liheap-energy-assistance/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/liheap-energy-assistance/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Weatherization Assistance Program (GEFA)</h3><p>Free whole-house energy efficiency improvements for income-qualified Georgia households: air and duct sealing, insulation, and HVAC upgrades that shrink future bills. The Georgia Environmental Finance Authority runs it through local community action agencies.</p><div><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-gefa/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-gefa/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Free &amp; Low-Cost Healthcare</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>PeachCare for Kids</h3><p>Georgia&#39;s CHIP: affordable health coverage for uninsured children up to age 18 whose families earn too much for Medicaid. DCH now charges no premiums for PeachCare; small copays of $0.50 to $12.50 apply for some services.</p><div><a href="/programs/peachcare-for-kids/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/peachcare-for-kids/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Cash Assistance &amp; Benefits</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>TANF Cash Assistance</h3><p>Monthly cash for very-low-income Georgia families with children under 18, and pregnant women. Apply at gateway.ga.gov or by paper Form 297 to your county DFCS office; adults are limited to 48 months in a lifetime.</p><div><a href="/programs/tanf-cash-assistance/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/tanf-cash-assistance/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Unemployment Insurance (GDOL)</h3><p>Georgia&#39;s unemployment benefits: temporary weekly payments if you lost work through no fault of your own. File online through the Georgia Department of Labor&#39;s MyUI Claimant Portal or at a local career center; the maximum duration adjusts between 14 and 26 weeks with the state unemployment rate.</p><div><a href="/programs/unemployment-insurance-gdol/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/unemployment-insurance-gdol/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div></section></div></section></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="American Aid Network home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>★</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>AMERICAN <b>AID</b><small>NETWORK</small></span></a><p>Clear, reliable guidance to assistance programs across America.</p><div class="verified">✓ Information from trusted sources</div></div><div><h4>FIND SUPPORT</h4><a href="/find/">Find help near me</a><a href="/help/">Browse by state</a><a href="/programs/">Program guides</a><a href="/#how-it-works">How it works</a></div><div><h4>ABOUT</h4><a href="/about/">Our mission</a><a href="/legal/contact/">Contact us</a><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="/legal/terms/">Terms of use</a></div></div><div class="wrap disclaimer">American Aid Network is an independent informational resource. We are not a government agency and do not administer benefit programs. Program details change; always confirm requirements with the official provider.<span>© 2026 American Aid Network</span></div></footer><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script></body></html>